      'Brunelleschi designed the dome as two shells, an inner structural one and an outer weatherproofing one, tied together by a system of stone and wood ribs, and he laid the brick in a distinctive herringbone spinapesce pattern that let each course lock into the ring below it and briefly support its ow.',
