      'Hooke, a contemporary and sometime collaborator of Wren\'s within the Royal Society, articulated the insight that a flexible chain hanging freely under its own weight naturally assumes a catenary curve in pure tension, and that an arch or dome built to the same curve, but working in compression ins.',
